From 5bcafab3d617eb718d317ef19e3f79675efbc228 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:33:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik(v2): isolate MDBX access and persist branch, asset
 and explorer indexes

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
No source semantics are added or removed by this history operation.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Extend Chronik with Lotus V2 3-branch script, token/asset ID, and
134-byte header indexers.

Original-Commit: 5ee9254cba0b0de4d25ba647d11c3af670832a58
Original-Patch: v2/012
Split-Concern: database

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Retain full V2 MDBX/index adapters while preserving first-owner fail-closed legacy RocksDB refusal and both original data-preservation regressions. Reconcile constructor return spelling with the new adapter; do not restore silent pseudo-migration or drop tests.

(cherry picked from commit 1ec8bdbaed20c4b30c3ca9c53c442863ae5d319b)

Canonical-Source-Commit: 1ec8bdbaed20c4b30c3ca9c53c442863ae5d319b

